22227</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="US-4421381-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>US</country><doc-number>4421381</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source name="APP" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="US-5748172-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>US</country><doc-number>5748172</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/><source name="APP" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1087248A1</text><sources><source name="APP" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ASADA NORIHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NIPPON SIGNAL CO LTD</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ASADA, NORIHIRO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>THE NIPPON SIGNAL CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ASADA NORIHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ASADA, NORIHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A planar optical scanner which is smaller and cheaper, and its mounting structure. A silicon wafer (11) is provided with a mirror (14) on the top surface side of a movable plate (12) pivotably supported by torsion bars (13A, 13B), a drive coil (15) on the rear surface side of the movable plate (12) to enable reduction of the area of the movable plate (12). A package substrate (31) is provided with a space (32) for allowing oscillation of the movable plate (12) and conductive patterns (33, 33A and 33B) in a region where an optical scanner is fixed, and the optical scanner (10) is mounted on the package substrate (31) with drive coil electrode terminals (16A, 16B) provided on the rear surface of the silicon wafer (11) in contact with the conductive patterns (33, 33A and 33B).</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un dispositif de balayage optique de type planar, plus petit et moins onéreux que les dispositifs de balayage optique de la technique antérieure. L'invention concerne également sa structure de montage. Selon l'invention, une tranche de silicium (11) présente un miroir (14) qui est placé sur la face supérieure d'une plaque mobile (12) supportée de manière pivotante par des barres de torsion (13A, 13B), ainsi qu'une bobine d'excitation (15) placée sur la face arrière de la plaque mobile (12) pour permettre une réduction de la surface de la plaque mobile (12). Un substrat d'encapsulation (31) présente un espace (32) permettant l'oscillation de la plaque mobile (12) ainsi que des tracés conducteurs (33, 33A et 33B) dans une zone où est fixé un dispositif de balayage optique. Ce dernier (10) est monté sur le substrat d'encapsulation (31) avec des bornes d'électrodes (16A, 16B) de la bobine d'excitation, placées sur la face arrière de la tranche de silicium (11) en contact avec les tracés conducteurs (33, 33A et 33B).</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml